        ],
        "path_description": "Three-hub network, not a single thread: Hub 1 (Smith-Spring frontier): Ngaru-Bon iron/charcoal flows south to Irrah; Irrah salt flows north to Ngaru-Bon. This is a frontier contact-point with buffer zone, not a through-route. Hub 2 (Irrah oasis network): internal east-west trunk corridors (The Spine) connecting 40+ oases. Hub 3 (Basin terminus): caravans depart Irrah westward under Qalībin escort to Halani-Tamu port on Basin's east shore",
        "commodities": "Salt, frankincense, myrrh, dates, silver outbound from Irrah to Basin; iron, grain, timber, cotton inbound from Basin/Ngaru-Bon to Irrah",
        "bottleneck": "Qalībin path-finders (only legally recognized desert escorts for the Basin leg); Smith-Spring buffer zone (neutral contact point for the Ngaru-Bon leg)",
        "consequence_if_closed": "Salt supply to southern continent collapses. Irrah iron imports cease. Continental banking network (khatti letters of credit) breaks — Qalībin oath-binders are the de facto banking infrastructure",
        "stroke": "#d4a854",
        "stroke-width": 2.5,
        "stroke-dasharray": "3,4"
